abstract: >-
  We establish three exact structural identities linking Hilbert spaces of entire
  functions, critical-line zero coalescence, and multiplicative prime-sieve gauges
  to the transverse Wronskian of Riemann's Xi-function. First, for the linear
  Hermite-Biehler family E_alpha(z) = Xi(z) - i*alpha*Xi'(z), the diagonal De Branges
  reproducing kernel satisfies K_alpha(t-id, t-id) = (alpha/pi)*W_tilde(d,t)
  everywhere in the complex plane. Second, at any critical-line zero of multiplicity
  m >= 1, all lower transverse dipole moments c_1(t_0), ..., c_{2m-3}(t_0) vanish
  while the leading coefficient collapses to the pure square
  c_{2m-1}(t_0) = [m/(m!)^2]*(Xi^{(m)}(t_0))^2 > 0, inducing a two-dimensional
  isotropic sum-of-squares bowl across any Lehmer pair. Third, for any real-analytic
  gauge multiplier M(z), we prove the universal Leibniz-Wronskian identity and combine
  it with a 0%-overshoot truncated Euler-product sieve to close the Lehmer uncertainty
  zone under the explicit Gabcke-Olver remainder bound.
